[[31,63,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(<a href=\"#/3025408\">5040</a> ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025427\">5040B14</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts fixing the pipe connectors.</p><p>2. Disconnect the connector from the drier filter.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Undo the  bracket retaining bolt.</p><p>4. Remove the bracket.</p><p>5. Recover the drier filter.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2004720.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. If necessary, undo the bolts fixing the support.</p><p>2. Remove the mount.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2004721.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the drier filter\nis intact and there are no signs of damage.</p><p>If removed, position the mount and fix\nit using the nuts.</p><p>Follow these precautions:</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Do not leave the filter with the\nconnectors disconnected for longer than is strictly necessary.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>- Use only green coloured seals,\nresistant to R134A coolant fluid.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>- Lubricate the threads of the\nconnectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>1. Connect the pipe connectors without tightening the fixing bolts.</p><p>2. Position the drier filter.</p><p>3. Position the bracket.</p><p>4. Tighten the bolt.</p><p>5. Tighten the bolts fixing the connectors to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT SYSTEM FITTINGS</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2004722.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3025427\">5040B14</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (<a href=\"#/3025410\">5040A10</a> ).</p>"],[16,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Observe the following precaution.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(<a href=\"#/3025408\">5040</a> ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p><a href=\"#/3025751\">7025A12</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025752\">7025A14</a></p><p>Drain the coolant (<a href=\"#/3024733\">0010T84</a> ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025916\">7055B64</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025911\">7055B42</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025960\">7210E10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts shown securing the duct.</p><p>2. Releaset he air duct retaining buttons using the special tool.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Scraper blade</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.823.015.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>3. Move the profile (3a) for the air duct slightly and undo the\nbolts (3b) underneath fastening the condenser.</p><p>4. Undo the plug for the drier filter container.</p><p>5. Release the retaining ring.</p><p>6. Move the condenser (6a) slightly forwards and extract the drier\nfilter cartridge (6b), after having tightened a threaded bolt for\nthe tool indicated below or an M12x1.75 screw in the opening.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Extractor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.842.134.000</p></td></tr></table></div><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the housing for the drier\nfilter cartridge using a suitable plug to prevent dampness and impurities\nfrom entering the system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2048800.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the drier filter cartridge is\nnot damaged.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.\nLubricate the thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Move the condenser slightly forwards and\nfit the drier filter cartridge.</p><p>Fit the retaining ring.</p><p>Tighten the drier filter container plug.</p><p>Tighten the bolts fixing the condenser.</p><p>Engage the retaining buttons for the air\nduct.</p><p>Tighten the bolts fixing the air duct.</p><p><a href=\"#/3025960\">7210E10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025911\">7055B42</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025916\">7055B64</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (<a href=\"#/3024733\">0010T84</a> ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3025752\">7025A14</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025751\">7025A12</a></p>"],[4,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Observe the following precaution.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(<a href=\"#/3025408\">5040</a> ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Drain the coolant (<a href=\"#/3024733\">0010T84</a> ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025916\">7055B64</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025911\">7055B42</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025960\">7210E10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts shown fastening the condenser.</p><p>2. Undo the plug for the drier filter container.</p><p>3. Release the retaining ring.</p><p>4. Move the condenser (4a) slightly forwards and extract the drier\nfilter cartridge (4b), tightening a threaded bolt for the tool indicated\nbelow or an M12x1.75 screw in the opening (4c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Extractor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.842.134.000</p></td></tr></table></div><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the housing for the drier\nfilter cartridge using a suitable plug to prevent dampness and impurities\nfrom entering the system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2048801.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the drier filter cartridge is\nnot damaged.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.\nLubricate the thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Move the condenser slightly forwards and\nfit the drier filter cartridge.</p><p>Fit the retaining ring.</p><p>Tighten the drier filter container plug.</p><p>Tighten the bolts fixing the condenser.</p><p><a href=\"#/3025960\">7210E10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025911\">7055B42</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025916\">7055B64</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025915\">7055B54</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (<a href=\"#/3024733\">0010T84</a> ).</p>"]]